---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import InnerOverlays from '../components/InnerOverlays.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Lab"
  description="Three small working tools: a NUBAN account-number checker, a demonstration of why money must be whole kobo, and a Brownian-motion visualiser."
>
  <main id="main" class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">home</a> / <span aria-current="page">lab</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="page-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Lab</span>
        <h1>Small things that run.</h1>
        <p>
          Three of the ideas behind my projects, small enough to try in the page. Everything here runs in your browser —
          nothing is sent anywhere.
        </p>
      </header>

      <article class="case">
        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>NUBAN account checker</span>
            <small>01</small>
          </h2>
          <p class="v-why">
            Nigerian account numbers carry a check digit. Work it out before you call the bank's API and you catch a
            mistyped account in the form, not after a failed transfer. This is the Central Bank's NUBAN rule: weights
            3·7·3 across the bank code and the first nine digits, then the check digit is what makes the total land on a
            multiple of ten.
          </p>
          <form class="tool" data-nuban>
            <div class="tool-fields">
              <div class="fld">
                <label for="nb-bank">
                  Bank code <i>*</i>
                </label>
                <input
                  id="nb-bank"
                  name="bank"
                  inputmode="numeric"
                  autocomplete="off"
                  maxlength="3"
                  placeholder="058"
                  required
                />
                <span class="err" data-err>
                  Three digits, for example 058.
                </span>
              </div>
              <div class="fld">
                <label for="nb-acct">
                  Account number <i>*</i>
                </label>
                <input
                  id="nb-acct"
                  name="acct"
                  inputmode="numeric"
                  autocomplete="off"
                  maxlength="10"
                  placeholder="0123456789"
                  required
                />
                <span class="err" data-err>
                  Ten digits.
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-actions">
              <button class="btn gold sm" type="submit">
                Check
              </button>
              <button class="btn sm" type="button" data-nuban-demo>
                Fill a valid example
              </button>
            </div>
            <output class="tool-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></output>
          </form>
          <p class="art-note">
            The check digit only proves the number is well formed. Whether the account exists, and whose it is, is still
            a question for the bank.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>Why money is whole kobo</span>
            <small>02</small>
          </h2>
          <p class="v-why">
            Every ledger I build stores money as an integer number of kobo, never a decimal. Here is the reason, in your
            own browser: add the same small amount again and again, once as a floating-point number of naira and once as
            whole kobo, and watch one of them drift.
          </p>
          <form class="tool" data-kobo>
            <div class="tool-fields">
              <div class="fld">
                <label for="kb-amt">Amount each time (₦)</label>
                <input id="kb-amt" name="amt" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" value="0.10" />
              </div>
              <div class="fld">
                <label for="kb-n">How many times</label>
                <input id="kb-n" name="n" type="number" min="1" max="1000000" step="1" value="10000" />
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-actions">
              <button class="btn gold sm" type="submit">
                Add them up
              </button>
            </div>
            <output class="tool-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></output>
          </form>
          <p class="art-note">
            The gap looks tiny. Across a day of transactions it is the difference between a ledger that balances and an
            afternoon spent finding one naira.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>Brownian motion</span>
            <small>03</small>
          </h2>
          <p class="v-why">
            The random walk behind option pricing, and the mathematics I studied before I wrote software for a living.
            Each line is one path: the same rules, a different roll of the dice. Change the volatility and watch the
            spread open up.
          </p>
          <div class="tool">
            <div class="tool-fields">
              <div class="fld">
                <label for="bm-paths">
                  Paths: <span data-bm-paths-val>12</span>
                </label>
                <input id="bm-paths" type="range" min="1" max="40" step="1" value="12" data-bm-paths />
              </div>
              <div class="fld">
                <label for="bm-vol">
                  Volatility: <span data-bm-vol-val>20%</span>
                </label>
                <input id="bm-vol" type="range" min="5" max="60" step="1" value="20" data-bm-vol />
              </div>
              <div class="fld">
                <label for="bm-steps">
                  Steps: <span data-bm-steps-val>250</span>
                </label>
                <input id="bm-steps" type="range" min="50" max="500" step="10" value="250" data-bm-steps />
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-actions">
              <button class="btn sm" type="button" data-bm-roll>
                Roll again
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="bm-wrap">
              <canvas data-bm-canvas width="900" height="420" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
            </div>
            <p class="sr">A drawing of the simulated paths. The numbers below describe the same result in words.</p>
            <output class="tool-out" data-bm-out aria-live="polite"></output>
          </div>
          <p class="art-note">
            A simulation, not a forecast. Nobody should price anything real from a canvas on a portfolio site.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="v-sec">
          <h2 class="v-h">
            <span>Want one of these for your product?</span>
            <small>04</small>
          </h2>
          <p>
            Account validation, a ledger that balances, or a model turned into something your team can actually use —
            that is the day job.
          </p>
          <div class="v-ctas">
            <a class="btn gold" href="/#contact">
              Get in touch
            </a>
            <a class="btn" href="/work/">
              See the projects
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <InnerOverlays slot="overlays" />
  <script src="../scripts/site.js"></script>
  <script src="../scripts/lab.js"></script>
</Base>
